                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "For a $6 game it is worth the money. The levels are fun and the mechanics are interesting. The best part of the game is the multiplayer. Coming up with better designs than your friends is challenging and competitive. It is a type of multiplayer you don't see too often.\n\nPro's:\n-Cheap\n-Easy to understand gameplay\n-Sandbox\n-Possibility to build complex things\n-Graphics are simple but still very pleasent to look at\n-Multiplayer with friends is very fun\n\nCon's:\n-Less than 20 singleplayer levels\n-Somewhat annoying gui and building becomes very tedious as there are no keyboard shortcuts\n-The game doesn't explain mechanics very well even though there is a tutorial (I had to make multiple google searches for an understanding of basic game mechanics)\n\nConclusion:\nIf you have an extra $6 in your steam wallet and are interested in getting a fun sandbox building game then get it. The game is fun for several hours but becomes a lot more worth if you and a friend both buy it as there are under 20 levels for singleplayer.",
